================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI AutomationListPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
over an injectable AutomationListDataSource seam whose value types mirror the KMP
presentation.automations Automation / AutomationBulkOp / AutomationBulkResult 1:1 (production binds
AutomationsStore.automations() + AutomationsStore.bulkAutomationsUpdate(ids:op:) through the seam).
The page reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle), the contextual bulk-action toolbar (selection
count + noun + of-total; Enable/Disable/Delete with per-op spinners; destructive Delete routed through
a confirmationDialog; Clear), and the single GlassPanel hosting an adaptive selectable table — a
columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-automation cards on iPhone — covering all five web columns
(select-all/row tri-state checkbox, name link, description, runs, enabled/disabled status badge) plus
the empty/loading/error states, using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass).
Bulk selection (toggle/select-all/tri-state/prune) is ported from web useBulkSelection and the bulk
runner from BulkActionToolbar + useBulkAutomationsUpdate (success clears + reloads; failure preserves
the selection and surfaces an alert). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with
the web key names (27 keys added). a11y: ≥44pt targets, VoiceOver isSelected/header/link traits,
Dynamic Type, light/dark + increased-contrast tokens. No value is unit-bearing, so no SI conversion
applies at this surface. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks
(macOS 0 / iOS 0) and an executed model harness (32/32). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due
to pervasive pre-existing, out-of-scope Swift 6.3 surface breakage (forbidden to commit-fix), with
ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

